From: Onuralp SEZER <thunderbirdtr@fedoraproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu7: isys: csi2: Handle a source sub-device that is gone

On the Dell XPS 16 DA16260 the OV08X40 sensor sits behind Intel CVS and
is powered through the Synaptics SVP7500 USB IO bridge. When that bridge
resets while the camera streams, the CVS sub-device is unbound and its
link to the CSI-2 receiver sink pad is removed. Stopping the stream then
dereferences the NULL remote pad in ipu7_isys_csi2_disable_streams():

  intel_ipu7_isys.isys intel_ipu7.isys.40: stream stop time out
  Oops: general protection fault, kernel NULL pointer dereference 0x20
  RIP: ipu7_isys_csi2_disable_streams+0x96/0x120 [intel_ipu7_isys]
   v4l2_subdev_disable_streams+0x215/0x3e0 [videodev]
   ipu7_isys_video_set_streaming+0x94/0x280 [intel_ipu7_isys]
   stop_streaming+0x100/0x130 [intel_ipu7_isys]
   __vb2_queue_cancel+0x2e/0x320 [videobuf2_common]

The task dies holding the stream locks, the process cannot be reaped and
only a reboot brings the camera back.

Skip the source when it is gone and still stop the receiver, and refuse
to start streaming without a source.

Signed-off-by: Onuralp SEZER <thunderbirdtr@fedoraproject.org>
---
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu7/ipu7-isys-csi2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu7/ipu7-isys-csi2.c
@@ -323,6 +323,9 @@ static int ipu7_isys_csi2_enable_streams(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	u32 sink_pad, sink_stream;
 	int ret, i;
 
+	if (!media_pad_remote_pad_first(&sd->entity.pads[IPU7_CSI2_PAD_SINK]))
+		return -ENOLINK;
+
 	if (!csi2->stream_count) {
 		dev_dbg(&csi2->isys->adev->auxdev.dev,
 			"stream on CSI2-%u with %u lanes\n", csi2->port,
@@ -379,10 +382,21 @@ static int ipu7_isys_csi2_disable_streams(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The source sub-device and its link are gone if the sensor was
+	 * unbound while streaming, e.g. when the USB IO bridge powering it
+	 * was reset. Still stop the receiver so the stream can be torn down.
+	 */
 	rp = media_pad_remote_pad_first(&sd->entity.pads[IPU7_CSI2_PAD_SINK]);
-	r_sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(rp->entity);
-
-	v4l2_subdev_disable_streams(r_sd, rp->index, BIT_ULL(sink_stream));
+	if (rp) {
+		r_sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(rp->entity);
+		v4l2_subdev_disable_streams(r_sd, rp->index,
+					    BIT_ULL(sink_stream));
+	} else {
+		dev_warn(&csi2->isys->adev->auxdev.dev,
+			 "CSI2-%u source is gone, stopping the receiver only\n",
+			 csi2->port);
+	}
 
 	if (--csi2->stream_count)
 		return 0;
